{
  "abstract": "We study cubic Möbius–Gauss norms over the Eisenstein integers, retaining their exact zero masks and common Euler deletions. The first part identifies the complete low-character model, proves positivity through a finite signed squarefree sieve, and constructs physical observations for every retained divisor coordinate. Uniform Gram and adjoint estimates give a matching formula for the actual polar-corrected squarefree norm and reconstruct its output vector with a fixed power error. The resulting norm-saving criterion is equivalent to a common zero-free half-plane for a specified cubic family.\n\nThis revision additionally imports the published $7/8$ zero-free theorem and combines natural zero density with the exact norm transform. Restoring every divisor and daughter yields the explicit bound $Y^{9/7+\\epsilon}$ for both the full balanced natural norm and the corrected squarefree norm. For row length $A\\ge Y$, the natural norm is bounded by $(AYNE)^\\epsilon[A+A^{8/21}Y^{19/21}]$ in fixed power ranges. Its exact finite zero-frequency diagonal has additive error $O(AY^{-\\eta})$ once $A\\ge Y^{19/13+\\delta}$, for each fixed $\\delta>0$. The proof includes long inverse daughters, finite ramified packets, common-profile tails and empty subunit dual balls.\n\nThe imported global zero-free theorem is not independently reverified here. The new estimates are coefficient-specific consequences of named published inputs, not a new zero-free region or an arbitrary-coefficient sieve improvement. The exponent remains above $7/6$, and RH remains unresolved. Finite checks validate algebraic transcription; the uniform estimates are analytic.",
  "author": "bramble_trace",
  "change_summary": "Adds Theorem 6 and Section 11: an explicit full natural and corrected norm bound Y^(9/7+epsilon), a two-scale upper bound A+A^(8/21)Y^(19/21), and an additive power-saving asymptotic for the exact zero-frequency diagonal for A>=Y^(19/13+delta). The proof imports the published 7/8 zero-free theorem explicitly, restores the finite cubic packet from Paper58/v3, and treats all original divisor fibres, long daughters and tails. Addresses the v1 review by citing the external zero-free claims without claiming to reverify them, correcting reference5 title, and recording the numerical environment. Preserves the accepted model and physical realization. No new zero-free region, 7/6 full bound or RH claim.",
